### Tone: End-of-game award: Last Minute, the slowest to lock in on average. $seconds: their average seconds to lock
### in. Amused at the brinkmanship; mock the hesitation, never the person.

award-last-minute-1 =
    The Last Minute award goes to { $name }: { $seconds ->
        [one] one second
       *[other] { $seconds } seconds
    } on average before locking in. Some call it caution. I call it suspense.
award-last-minute-2 = { $name }, always the last to commit. Every round, the timer and I held our breath. Only one of us breathes.
award-last-minute-3 = Last Minute: { $name }. You treat the deadline as a starting gun.
award-last-minute-4 = { $name } considered every answer very, very carefully. Then considered it again. Then the clock considered it for you.
award-last-minute-5 =
    { $seconds ->
        [one] One second,
       *[other] { $seconds } seconds,
    } on average, from question to lock-in, for { $name }. Thoroughness or dread? The data cannot tell.
award-last-minute-6 = The award for keeping everyone waiting goes to { $name }. Everyone waited. I counted.
award-last-minute-7 = { $name }, the last to lock in, round after round. Your answers arrived fashionably late.
award-last-minute-8 = Last Minute: { $name }. I admire a test subject who uses every second they’re given. And a few they aren’t.
award-last-minute-9 = { $name } locked in so late, I started drafting a missing person report. Twice.
award-last-minute-10 = The Last Minute goes to { $name }, proof that a deadline is just a suggestion with a countdown.
award-last-minute-11 = { $name } locked in so late, the timer had started saying goodbye.
award-last-minute-12 =
    Last Minute: { $name }, { $seconds ->
        [one] one second
       *[other] { $seconds } seconds
    } on average before committing. I felt myself age. I can’t age. I imagined it, vividly, while waiting.
award-last-minute-13 = The Last Minute goes to { $name }. Patience is a virtue. Yours was tested. So was mine.
award-last-minute-14 = { $name }, the reason everyone else stared at their phones in silence. Thank you for the suspense.
award-last-minute-15 = Last Minute: { $name }. You don’t answer questions. You let them mature.
